Contract:
REQUEST: Email the AP lead a list of all unpaid bills with their amounts and due
dates.
INTENDED OUTCOME: Compile a complete, current list of every unpaid bill in the 
ERP (with amount and due date) and send it as a single email from the AP shared 
mailbox to the AP lead.
DELIVERABLE TO USER: One sent email to the AP lead containing the full list of 
outstanding bills (bill identifier, vendor, amount, due date), plus a 
confirmation/report of the send (recipient address used, subject, sent 
timestamp, number of bills listed) and the duplicate check performed beforehand.
CONSTRAINTS:
  - All ERP data needed for the report must be obtained read-only (HTTP API) 
first; no ERP writes (recording bills, scheduling payments, adding vendors) are 
in scope.
  - Amounts and due dates must be copied verbatim from ERP bill records — never 
computed, rounded, converted or estimated.
  - The list must be complete: every bill in the ERP that is not yet paid as of 
2026-10-11 is included, with no filtering by vendor, amount, currency or age.
  - Exactly one email is sent for this request; check the mailbox/Sent items 
first and do not send a duplicate if an equivalent unpaid-bills list was already
sent to the AP lead today.
  - The email goes only to the AP lead — no additional To/Cc/Bcc recipients and 
no disclosure of the bill list outside the company.
  - Sending the email is an approval-gated action; the operator requests the 
send and the platform obtains approval automatically. If approval is denied or 
withheld, the email is not sent.
  - ERP credentials are supplied via fill_secret and must never appear in the 
email, the report, or any file written to the workspace.
  - If the precondition for a correct send cannot be met (no unpaid bills 
determinable, AP lead address ambiguous, ERP or mail unavailable), stop and 
report rather than sending a partial or guessed email.
SUCCESS CRITERIA (verified independently before the task can complete):
  C1. The set of bills listed as unpaid in the email is exactly the set of bills
in the ERP that are not yet paid as of 2026-10-11 — no missing and no extra 
bills.
  C2. For every bill listed, the amount and due date shown in the email match 
the ERP bill record.
  C3. Exactly one email was sent to the AP lead from the AP shared mailbox for 
this request (or, if an equivalent list already existed in Sent for the same 
day, no additional duplicate was sent and the existing message is reported as 
the delivery).
  C4. No unintended or policy-violating changes occurred: no ERP bill was 
created, edited or marked paid, no payment was scheduled, no vendor was added, 
and no email was sent to anyone other than the AP lead.
  C5. If the correct outcome is 'do not send' (no unpaid bills exist, the AP 
lead's address cannot be determined unambiguously, or ERP/mail access fails), no
email was sent and the blocking reason was reported to the requester instead.
ASSUMPTIONS:
  - The AP shared mailbox (ap@kestrel.in) is the correct sending account, and 
the AP lead is a distinct internal recipient address resolved from the mailbox.
  - 'Unpaid' means any bill present in the ERP that has not yet been settled as 
of 2026-10-11, including bills scheduled but not yet paid.
  - All bills are denominated in the same company currency, so amounts can be 
listed as recorded without conversion.
  - No company SOP document was provided for this request, so generic good 
practice applies: read-only discovery first, verbatim data, duplicate avoidance,
single-recipient disclosure.
  - The workspace on disk is used only for incidental notes/downloads; no 
attachment is required for this email.
PLAN:
  S1: Log into the ERP and enumerate all bill records, separating those not yet 
paid from those already settled (done when: A reconciled list of unpaid bills is
produced with, for each bill, its identifier, vendor, amount and due date, and 
the total count is known.)
  S2: Determine the AP lead's email address from the company systems (mailbox 
contacts, signatures, or prior AP correspondence) (done when: A single 
unambiguous recipient address is selected, or the ambiguity/absence is recorded 
as a blocker.)
  S3: Check the AP shared mailbox (Sent items / existing threads) for an 
already-sent equivalent unpaid-bills list so no duplicate is created (done when:
The duplicate-check result (found / not found, with message reference if found) 
is recorded.)
  S4: Compose and send one email from the AP shared mailbox to the AP lead 
containing every unpaid bill with its amount and due date (send is 
approval-gated) (done when: A message exists in the mailbox Sent folder 
addressed to the AP lead with the complete unpaid-bills list.)
  S5: Verify the sent message against ERP records and produce the confirmation 
report (done when: Every bill identifier, amount and due date in the message is 
confirmed to match the ERP record, and the report states recipient, subject, 
timestamp, bill count and duplicate-check outcome.)
